.TH NETSTUDIO-HEADLESS 1 "2026" "netstudio-headless 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
netstudio-headless \- run the NetStudio probing engine without the desktop app
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netstudio-headless
\-\-config
.I PATH
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B netstudio-headless
probes the targets listed in a NetStudio JSON configuration file (ICMP, TCP,
HTTP, HTTPS) and reports latency, jitter, loss and status. It has three modes:
a one-shot probe
.RB ( \-\-once ),
a preflight validation
.RB ( \-\-check ),
and a daemon that streams snapshots, writes a status file and serves HTTP for
health checks, Prometheus scraping and the alert feed.
.PP
The daemon stops gracefully on SIGINT/SIGTERM and reloads its configuration on
SIGHUP (Unix).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Target configuration file. Required for every mode.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Validate the file, the
.B \-\-output
and
.B \-\-pid-file
paths and the
.B \-\-listen
address, then exit without probing.
.TP
.BI \-\-health\-check " " URL
Send one GET to URL (http:// only) and exit 0 only on 200, 1 on another status
or a transport error, 2 for an unusable URL. Needs no config; the token comes
from
.B \-\-http\-token\-file
or NETSTUDIO_HTTP_TOKEN. For container health checks.
.TP
.B \-\-once
Probe every target once, print a snapshot, and exit. Exit status 3 means at
least one non-muted target is down.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " " SECS
Snapshot interval in seconds, 1 to 3600 (default 5).
.TP
.BI \-\-probe\-interval " " SECS
Probe every target this often, overriding each target's own interval_ms.
.TP
.BI \-\-probe\-concurrency " " N
Maximum probes in flight, 1 to 256 (default 32).
.TP
.BI \-\-watch\-config " " SECS
Poll the config file every 1 to 3600 seconds and reload it when it changes.
Daemon mode only; useful where SIGHUP cannot be delivered.
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " " ADDR
Serve HTTP on ADDR, for example
.IR 127.0.0.1:9101 .
Daemon mode only; see
.B HTTP ENDPOINTS
below.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " " PATH
Atomically replace PATH with the latest JSON snapshot.
.TP
.BI \-\-pid\-file " " PATH
Claim PATH exclusively, write the pid and remove it on a graceful stop.
Daemon mode only.
.TP
.BI \-\-http\-token\-file " " PATH
Require "Authorization: Bearer <token>" on every HTTP endpoint except
/healthz; the token is read from PATH. Daemon mode only.
.TP
.BR \-\-windows\-service
Let the Windows Service Control Manager own the process. Daemon mode, Windows
only; started from a shell it exits 2 instead of probing invisibly.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Do not stream snapshots to stdout. The HTTP endpoints and
.B \-\-output
keep working.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " " MODE
.IR auto " (default: text on a terminal, JSON when piped), " json " or " text .
.TP
.BI \-\-color " " WHEN
.IR auto " (default), " always " or " never .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Same as
.BR "\-\-color never" .
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " " LEVEL
.IR error ", " warn ", " info " (default) or " debug .
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-format " " FMT
.IR text " (default) or " json
for one JSON object per stderr line.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file " " PATH
Append every log line to PATH as well as stderr. Rotated to PATH.1 at 8 MiB
and never truncated on restart; a Windows service has no stderr to read.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NETSTUDIO_HTTP_TOKEN
Bearer token used when
.B \-\-http\-token\-file
is not given.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable ANSI colour, like
.BR "\-\-color never" .
.SH HTTP ENDPOINTS
Served on
.B \-\-listen .
Everything but
.I /healthz
needs the
.B \-\-http\-token\-file
bearer token when one is configured.
.TP
.I /healthz
Always open, for container and systemd probes.
.TP
.I /readyz
503 until every target has one sample.
.TP
.I /metrics
Prometheus text format.
.TP
.I /api/v1/status
The latest snapshot as JSON.
.TP
.I /api/v1/events?since=\fISEQ\fR
Alert feed: the
.B down
and
.B up
transitions after SEQ, with a monotonic cursor and a count of any the
buffer dropped.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the config file and re-read
.B \-\-http\-token\-file
without a restart (Unix).
.B \-\-watch\-config
provides the same reload where SIGHUP is unavailable.
.TP
.B SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Graceful stop: cancel probes, close the HTTP listener and remove the pid
file. On Windows, console Ctrl+C does the same.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; with
.B \-\-once
every probed target answered.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure after startup.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid configuration or command line, unusable output/pid path, or an
address that cannot be bound.
.TP
.B 3
.B \-\-once
finished with at least one non-muted target down.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/netstudio/targets.json
Common location for the target file in deployments. Its keys, types and
ranges are described by
.IR docs/netstudio-headless.schema.json ;
an unknown key is reported and ignored, and an unknown
.B protocol
skips the target rather than falling back to ICMP.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
netstudio-headless \-c targets.json \-\-check
Preflight a configuration and its paths.
.TP
netstudio-headless \-c targets.json \-q \-\-output /var/lib/netstudio/status.json \\
\-\-listen 127.0.0.1:9101 \-\-pid\-file /run/netstudio/headless.pid
Run the daemon with a status file and Prometheus endpoint.
.SH SEE ALSO
The full documentation and example configuration in
.IR docs/headless.md " and " docs/examples/targets.json .
